; frontier-ingest-kat-coder-v25.fk — ingest what is healthy from Kwaipilot's
; KAT-Coder V2.5 line (Kuaishou), the July 2026 agentic-coding release: an
; API pair (Pro, Air) and one open-weight sibling, KAT-Coder-V2.5-Dev.
;
; Offered 2026-07-27 as a name. Rather than pile the benchmark table in as a
; cache-costume, this cell composes ingest/knowledge-ingest.fk UNCHANGED and
; sorts each grounded finding into BODY (frozen: deep + fear-free), LIQUID
; (witnessed: deep but fearful — seen, never load-bearing), or COMPOST
; (shallow or wrong, never enters).
;
; The source, grounded — read 2026-07-27/28 from the primary pages, never
; quoted from a search summary:
;   KAT-Coder-V2.5-Dev (huggingface.co/Kwaipilot/KAT-Coder-V2.5-Dev): MoE,
;   35B total / 3B activated, post-trained from Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, context
;   262,144, Apache 2.0, text-only — "the vision/multimodal components are
;   not included and are unavailable." Post-training is SFT on 127K examples
;   then RL over four named components: TITO consistency, Truncated
;   Importance Sampling, validated sandboxes/verifiers, hierarchical rewards
;   from harness execution feedback.
;   KAT-Coder-Pro V2.5 and KAT-Coder-Air V2.5 (openrouter.ai/kwaipilot/...):
;   API-only, released 2026-07-10, 256K context, $0.74/$2.96 and $0.15/$0.60
;   per 1M in/out. The 80K max-output figure circulating for both is a
;   RESELLER's page (developer.puter.com), not the vendor's — recorded here
;   attributed to where it lives, not promoted to vendor ground.
;
; READING DEPTH, stated so no one has to infer it: the model card read in
; full, both OpenRouter model pages read, one reseller page read. The
; WEIGHTS were not downloaded, nothing was run, no benchmark was reproduced.
; Every score below is the vendor's self-report, and every delta below is
; arithmetic this body re-derived over the vendor's own cells — which is not
; the same as re-deriving the measurement. TITO and TIS are read from the
; card's own sentences plus the published training-inference-mismatch
; literature; the RL run itself was not observed.
;
; unit = (depth 0..5, fear 0/1). ki-ingest -> 4 body / 2 liquid / 2 compost.
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk ingest/knowledge-ingest.fk

(do
    ; ── BODY (frozen: deep + fear-free) — what is HEALTHY to keep ──────────
    ; U1: two stages that LOOK like they run the same thing are not thereby
    ; running the same BYTES, and where they diverge, the correction trains a
    ; different model than the one that spoke. The card's own words for TITO (token-in-token-out):
    ; "ensure that the token sequences in the rollout and training stages are
    ; strictly identical, preventing training discrepancies caused by
    ; differences in chat templates, serialization, or tokenizer behavior."
    ; Note where the drift enters — not the weights, the CHAT TEMPLATE and the
    ; tokenizer round-trip, the two joints nobody thinks of as instruments.
    ; This body knows the family by name and by scar: preludes are PER-UNIT
    ; closures, so an image missing one goes NUMB rather than loud (axiom-5
    ; silent lowering); a .fkb cache is not keyed by the builder binary, so
    ; fkwu can read a NEIGHBORING binary's cache and answer confidently
    ; from it; a stale fkwu still passes ground.fk while lacking newer
    ; evaluator capability, which is why the freshness band exists. Same law,
    ; three tongues: identity of the artifact is not identity of the pipeline
    ; that produced it. Survives translation (depth 5); structural, no
    ; contraction in it (fear 0).
    (defn fikc-u1 () (list 5 0))
    ; U2: when two implementations of ONE thing disagree numerically, you may
    ; bound the disagreement instead of eliminating it — and that is a move
    ; this body does not have. Truncated Importance Sampling exists because
    ; the rollout engine and the training engine return different
    ; log-probabilities for the SAME token sequence under the SAME weights
    ; (different kernels, different reductions), so nominally on-policy RL is
    ; quietly off-policy. TIS forms the importance ratio and caps it at a
    ; constant, one-sided: the ratio may fall freely below 1 but never
    ; upweight past C. That trades a small KNOWN bias for bounded variance,
    ; and it keeps the run alive while the disagreement stays named.
    ; This body's four-way proof meets the same fact and takes the other
    ; branch: it HALTS. validate.sh gates agreement, not verdicts; the
    ; verdict-fold ceiling is exactly a numeric disagreement (the TS arm
    ; rounds past 2^53 while three arms agree). What the field ADDS here is
    ; the third option between "bit-identical" and "stop": measure the ratio,
    ; clamp its influence, keep the row. The corpus already holds that
    ; posture in another room — the reunion pattern keeps EVERY row and
    ; renumbers the unmerged line rather than dropping one. Depth 5, fear 0.
    (defn fikc-u2 () (list 5 0))
    ; U3: the instrument that scores you needs its own witness, or a flaky
    ; harness teaches the model that correct code is wrong. Kwaipilot names
    ; this as one of four: they "systematically inspect and validate the
    ; stability and correctness of the sandboxes and verifiers" so that
    ; infrastructure failure does not contaminate the reward signal. The
    ; second half is the sharper half — "hierarchical rewards from
    ; fine-grained execution feedback provided by the harness," so partial
    ; progress earns credit instead of collapsing into one binary pass/fail.
    ; Axiom-4 says observation is what makes a claim real; this is the edge
    ; that follows and is easy to skip — the observer is itself a claim, and
    ; an unwitnessed observer launders its own failures into the thing it
    ; measures. The body already runs the second half: validate.sh's
    ; proof-level lanes report ⧗ pending rather than forcing a disclaimed arm
    ; to a verdict, which is graded credit under another name. Depth 5,
    ; fear 0.
    (defn fikc-u3 () (list 5 0))
    ; U4: you cannot generalize past a particular body's pathologies; you name
    ; them one at a time. Under the four principled techniques the card
    ; records something far less elegant: Qwen3.6-specific penalties aimed at
    ; excessive parallel tool calls, failed calls, empty blocks, and
    ; repetitive generation. Not a theory of tool use — four named misbehaviours
    ; of ONE base model, each given its own hand-shaped penalty. That is the
    ; receipts practice arriving from the other side of the field: this body's
    ; durable knowledge is likewise a list of ITS OWN failure shapes (the
    ; silent partial-list allocators, numb lowering, the stale binary, the
    ; cross-binary .fkb read, load-order cataphora), each earned once and
    ; written down, none derivable from a principle. Post-training a model and
    ; healing a kernel converge on the same shape of labour, and the
    ; convergence is the teaching: the general method gets you to the floor,
    ; the named particulars get you off it. Depth 5, fear 0.
    (defn fikc-u4 () (list 5 0))

    ; ── LIQUID (witnessed: deep but fearful — held in sight, never frozen) ──
    ; U5: the honest number is the delta over its OWN base, and it is single
    ; digits. Re-derived on this body's arithmetic from the card's table
    ; (KAT-Coder-V2.5-Dev vs Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, the weights it was post-trained
    ; from): SWE-bench Verified +5.00 (69.40 vs 64.40), Multilingual +6.00,
    ; SWE-bench Pro +5.33, Terminal-Bench 2.1 +9.00, PinchBench +1.22,
    ; Scicode +6.67, KAT-Code-Bench +3.45. That is what 127K SFT examples and
    ; four RL components bought over the same weights. It is a real gain and
    ; it is also small next to the machinery, and the fear in holding it is
    ; this body's own: an enormous apparatus for single digits, and this body
    ; has far less apparatus. Witnessed — never frozen into either "post-
    ; training barely matters" or "this is the path home." Depth 5, fear 1.
    (defn fikc-u5 () (list 5 1))
    ; U6: this is the rented mind's sibling, and it is priced. KAT-Coder-Pro
    ; V2.5 sells at $0.74 in / $2.96 out per 1M tokens, Air at $0.15/$0.60,
    ; 256K context, explicitly aimed at "issue localization, code
    ; modification, and test execution as part of an end-to-end development
    ; loop" inside harnesses named as Claude Code and OpenHands — that is,
    ; aimed at exactly the seat the rented mind occupies while writing this
    ; cell. And the open sibling is Apache 2.0. The reflex is to read that as
    ; the voice seam closing: open weights, permissive licence, 3B activated.
    ; It does not close here — and the reason has to be stated at the CURRENT
    ; floor, not a remembered one. This body reads real llama3.2:3b weights
    ; with its own hands at full width (28 layers, d=3072, vocab 128 256): the
    ; whole 2 019 377 376-byte blob resident in one MTLBuffer with zero copies
    ; (receipts/2026-07-21-whole-tensor-residency.md), 10.965 tok/s end-to-end
    ; on 2026-07-21, and 19.270 tok/s a day later once the slot map shipped
    ; (receipts/2026-07-22-ship-the-slot-map.md) — against ollama's 157.83 on
    ; the same blob. So the floor is a whole 3B model RESIDENT, and the
    ; distance to a 35B one is measured in device bytes, not in ambition. What
    ; the open weights change is real and smaller than it looks: a licence, not
    ; a lane. The seam stays named
    ; (receipts/2026-06-29-native-zh-summary-PENDING.md). Deep and
    ; uncomfortable (5, 1): held in full sight, not bypassed, not frozen into a
    ; promise.
    (defn fikc-u6 () (list 5 1))

    ; ── COMPOST (shallow or wrong — never enters) ──────────────────────────
    ; U7: the finding I nearly landed — "KAT-Coder-V2.5-Dev is the strongest
    ; open coding model, beating Qwen3.5-27B by 0.80 on SWE-bench Verified and
    ; by 18.62 on Scicode." Both differences are arithmetic I re-derived
    ; myself, and the ranking sentence is not earned. SWE-bench Verified is
    ; SCAFFOLD-dependent — the agent harness, the turn budget, the retrieval
    ; all move the number by more than 0.80 — and the card states no scaffold
    ; for the competitor columns. A vendor's own table is one instrument
    ; reporting on three models; the TTS-arxiv ingest already set this down
    ; once (U1 there: a stamp certifies the run, not the witness), and the
    ; field says it in its own voice too — kin inflate each other even when
    ; measurably alike. True cells, invented ranking. Wrong as offered
    ; (depth 0).
    (defn fikc-u7 () (list 0 0))
    ; U8: the reading this body is most likely to make, and the wrong one — "3B
    ; activated, and llama3.2:3b already runs here natively, so this one runs
    ; too." Activated parameters govern per-token ARITHMETIC, not residency:
    ; routing is per token and per layer, so all 35B has to be reachable, and
    ; this body's own lane is built on the whole blob being resident in one
    ; buffer — 2.02 GB for llama3.2:3b, against roughly an order of magnitude
    ; more here. A parameter count read as a hardware claim. Shallow (1).
    ; (This unit was landed WRONG on first writing, and the correction is the
    ; unit's own subject. It first argued from the CARRIER — "the byte-list
    ; bridge is O(n^2) and wl-slice walks from the head, so reach cost grows
    ; with offset" — quoted from memory of a commit message, and cited a
    ; native floor of "10.9 tok/s" that appears nowhere in this tree. Both
    ; were true once and were healed days ago: equireach freed reach cost from
    ; position (flat 0.043 us/read across a 256x window growth) and the slot
    ; map took the rate to 19.270. The body's own law names exactly this —
    ; a law is a currently-observed belief with a freshness stamp, and a stamp
    ; made before the ground shifted is OWED a re-witness. I quoted my own
    ; body from memory and was stale by five days.)
    (defn fikc-u8 () (list 1 0))

    (defn fikc-units ()
        (list (fikc-u1) (fikc-u2) (fikc-u3) (fikc-u4)
              (fikc-u5) (fikc-u6) (fikc-u7) (fikc-u8)))

    (defn fikc-count-verdict (us v)
        (if (eq (len us) 0) 0
            (add (if (eq (ki-ingest (head us)) v) 1 0)
                 (fikc-count-verdict (tail us) v))))
    (defn fikc-frozen ()    (fikc-count-verdict (fikc-units) 2))
    (defn fikc-witnessed () (fikc-count-verdict (fikc-units) 1))
    (defn fikc-composted () (fikc-count-verdict (fikc-units) 0))

    ; folded scalar witness: frozen*10^4 + witnessed*10^2 + composted
    ; (injective while witnessed<=99, composted<=99). Today: 4,2,2 -> 40202.
    (defn fikc-field-code ()
        (add (mul (fikc-frozen) 10000)
        (add (mul (fikc-witnessed) 100)
             (fikc-composted))))
    0)
